    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "The function updateUserBalance does not ascertain the duration for which a user has retained the token. Exploiting this, the attacker pre-deploys numerous malicious contracts, secures the initial $VTF via a flashloan, and subsequently transfers the VTF tokens to each attack contract sequentially. This maneuver enables the attacker to claim the rewards for holding. Vulnerable code snippet: https://bscscan.com/address/0xc6548caf18e20f88cc437a52b6d388b0d54d830d#code Attack tx: https://bscscan.com/tx/0xeeaf7e9662a7488ea724223c5156e209b630cdc21c961b85868fe45b64d9b086 https://bscscan.com/tx/0xc2d2d7164a9d3cfce1e1dac7dc328b350c693feb0a492a6989ceca7104eef9b7 Analysis: https://twitter.com/BlockSecTeam/status/1585575129936977920 https://twitter.com/peckshield/status/1585572694241988609 https://twitter.com/BeosinAlert/status/1585587030981218305"
    }
